# Accepted image-scan findings. Every entry needs a reason and an expiry date;
# Trivy reports the finding again once the date passes.

# The four entries below are libraries vendored inside pip 26.2.1 (pip/_vendor/vendor.txt)
# in the pip-audit tool environment at /opt/uv-tools/pip-audit. pip-audit needs pip to
# resolve requirements targets, 26.2.1 is the latest pip release, and the installed
# msgpack/urllib3 packages in both environments are already the fixed versions
# (docker/agent-runtime-constraints.txt). Remove these once pip ships updated vendored copies.

# msgpack 1.1.2: out-of-bounds read on Unpacker reuse (pip only unpacks its own HTTP cache)
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2027-01-31
# msgpack 1.1.2: memory leak during map deserialization (pip 26.2.2 still vendors 1.1.2)
CVE-2026-114613 exp:2027-01-31
# setuptools 70.3.0: path traversal in PackageIndex.download (pip does not use PackageIndex)
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2027-01-31
# urllib3 2.7.0: pip's vendored HTTP client
CVE-2026-97687 exp:2027-01-31
CVE-2026-97689 exp:2027-01-31

# Guava 33.4.6 (/opt/gradle/lib) and 33.6.0 (/opt/maven/lib) ship inside the Gradle 9.8.2
# and Maven 3.9.16 distributions, the latest releases of both. The DoS needs Guava to
# deserialize attacker-supplied data, which the build tools do not do. Remove this once
# either tool bundles Guava 33.7.2 or later.
CVE-2026-102554 exp:2027-01-31
